SUMMARY:Intergenerational Nature Hike and Picnic
DESCRIPTION:All are welcome for a joyful day of fellowship\, food\, and time in nature! Our potluck picnic is open to everyone! \nAt 11:00 AM\, hikers will set off with a park naturalist for a guided walk\, while those who prefer to stay at the pavilion are invited to enjoy a presentation from The Grange on the science of soil management\, crop production\, and responsible agricultural practices. This engaging discussion will explore farming in the United States over the past 250 years and look ahead to its future. \nWhen the hikers return\, we’ll gather for lunch. The Mission & Justice Committee will provide and grill hamburgers and hot dogs. Bring a dish to share. \nRain or shine\, come enjoy time together with your Saint James family! \nClick here to register.
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/intergenerational-nature-hike-and-picnic/
LOCATION:Lancaster County Park\, 1098 Rockford Rd\,\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Featured-Image-Hiking-Image-copy.jpg
GEO:40.0242216;-76.2967165
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Lancaster County Park 1098 Rockford Rd Lancaster PA 17602;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=1098 Rockford Rd\,:geo:-76.2967165,40.0242216
END:VEVENT
